"best_output_degree":5,"central_binomial":126,"exact_term_denominator":15046709021474156741571640,"glynn_upper":256,"integer_route_ceiling":225,"source_target_cap_numerator":3371940002777708686289731920}},"status":["GENERAL_HIGHER_KOSZUL_CHOW_TERM_RANK","GENERAL_LOW_WEDGE_COMPLEXITY_BARRIER","EXACT_INTEGER_REPLAYED"],"theorem":{"complexity_gate":"If r=o(n log n), the route is n^(o(1))*C(n,floor(n/2))=o(2^(n-1)). If r=o(n^2), reaching Glynn scale requires r>=(1/2-o(1))*n*log n.","duality":"R_(n,d,p)=R_(n,n-d+1,n^2-p-1).","exact_rank":"R_(n,d,p)=sum_q C(n^2-n,p-q) sum_h C(n,h) C(n-h,d+q-2h) C(d+q-2h-1,d-h-1).","homology_recurrence":"R_(n,d,p)+R_(n,d+1,p-1)=C(n,d)[C(n^2,p)-C(n^2-n,p-d)].","low_wedge_ceiling":"With r=min(p,n^2-p-1)<=n^2-n, every single higher-Koszul rank-ratio route is at most C(n,floor(n/2))*C(n^2,r)/C(n^2-n,r)."}}